{"findings":[{"finding":"The open-status list has no built-in value and an empty list silently means 'no invoice is ever overdue', but nothing covers a missing or empty setting at deployment (no startup failure, no error), so a misconfiguration gives an empty overdue list that looks correct.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"The staff claim type and value have no built-in value, but nothing says what happens when they are not configured (startup failure, every request 403, or every request allowed), and no AC covers it.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Q-1 says 'any authenticated staff user, using the existing API's authentication', but REQ-19 assumes the existing API's tokens carry a claim that tells staff from non-staff, and current-behaviour has no claims to back that up, so this new 403 gate may block every real user.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-1.1 to AC-1.5 and AC-1.7 are checked only through the internal OverduePolicy.Evaluate method (unit level), not through GET /api/invoices/overdue, so the overdue rule, the time-zone boundary and the status filter are never shown at the public API.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Only a known customer with no invoices is covered (AC-3.1 returns an empty 200); nothing says what happens with a customerId that does not exist or is badly formed (e.g. not a valid ID type), unlike the 400 that REQ-4 defines for a bad bucket.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No failure path is defined for when the client's existing database or invoice source adapter cannot be reached or returns bad rows (e.g. an invoice with a missing customer), and there is no AC for a 200 with an empty list when nothing is overdue at all.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'Return every invoice currently classified as overdue' has no ordering or pagination, even though NFR-1 expects 5,000+ open invoices, so the size and order of the response cannot be tested.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The actual query-string values for the buckets are never given: the ACs use en-dash labels ('7–30', '61+') while AC-4.3's invalid example uses a hyphen ('5-6'), so the accepted daysOverdue token format is unclear at the API.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The assumptions say an invalid token (bad signature, wrong issuer) gets 401, but AC-14.1 only tests no token and an expired token.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"daysOverdue for an invoice not yet due (due date after today) is not defined (negative, zero or left out), even though Evaluate returns daysOverdue for invoices that are not overdue (AC-1.1 returns 6).","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The text says both billing emails and invoice amounts stay out of logs, but the metric only counts billing emails, which this run never reads (sending is in Run 2), so the check passes by default; amounts and customer names, which this run does return, are not checked.","reqId":"NFR-3","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The 10,000-invoice / 5,000-open volume is justified only as 'the largest data volume any draft gave', with no link to an answer, assumption or the client's real data.","reqId":"NFR-1","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-2.2's 'no overdue flag was written to the invoice record' and AC-1.6's 'invoice record unchanged' need a direct check of the client's database, which is not a public surface of this API.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Overdue is computed on every request by reading the client's live production Postgres directly through an adapter, but nothing limits query load or the access level (read-only role) on the client's existing database.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":7,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The accepted assumptions ASM-5 (later bounces count as failures) and ASM-13 (only immediate send errors count) contradict each other, and the spec silently picks ASM-13 in outOfScope without saying the conflict was settled.","rubric":1,"severity":"low"}],"note":"No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"}